          <caption>
            <p>Electrocardiogram Showing Inferior ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction With Right Ventricular Involvement. This 12-lead electrocardiogram demonstrates ST-segment elevation in leads II, III, and aVF, indicating an acute inferior wall myocardial infarction. ST elevation in lead III greater than in lead II suggests right coronary artery occlusion with possible right ventricular myocardial infarction. ST-segment elevation in V1, with or without V2, during an inferior ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction indicates concomitant right ventricular involvement. Contributed by William Gossman, MD, FAAEM</p>
          </caption>
